{0 A client session}

This page reads one program that connects to a server, selects a
mailbox, searches it, fetches metadata and archives the matches. The
program is [test/examples/client.ml], which the build compiles and never
runs, and every block below is copied from it.

{1 Connecting}

{!Imap_eio.Transport.v} names the server, with implicit TLS on port 993
by default. {!Imap_eio.Auth.password} holds a fixed password, and over
TLS its default mechanism prefers advertised SASL PLAIN, then CRAM-MD5,
then LOGIN. {!Imap_eio.Client.connect} opens the connection, checks the
certificate, reads the greeting and authenticates.

{!Imap_eio.Client.with_mailbox} selects [INBOX] and holds the selection
lease across the callback. The lease handle expires when the callback
returns. A [Client] call on the same connection from inside the callback
is [Error (State _)] and sends nothing, so the callback uses only the
[Selected] operations. {!Imap_eio.Client.logout} ends the session and
releases the transport even when it fails.

{[
let () =
  Eio_main.run @@ fun env ->
  Eio.Switch.run @@ fun sw ->
  let transport =
    Imap_eio.Transport.v ~net:(Eio.Stdenv.net env) ~host:"imap.example.org" ()
  in
  let auth =
    Imap_eio.Auth.password ~username:"alice" ~password:"secret" ()
  in
  let result =
    let* client = Imap_eio.Client.connect ~sw ~auth transport in
    match
      Imap_eio.Client.with_mailbox client ~mode:`Read_write "INBOX"
        archive_old
    with
    | Ok () -> Imap_eio.Client.logout client
    | Error _ as error ->
        Imap_eio.Client.close client;
        error
  in
  match result with
  | Ok () -> ()
  | Error e ->
      Format.eprintf "imap: %a@." Imap_eio.Client.pp_error e;
      exit 1
]}

{1 Searching and fetching}

{!Imap_eio.Selected.uid_search} takes typed {!Imap.Search.t} criteria
and is the matching UIDs, sorted and without duplicates.
{!Imap_eio.Selected.fetch} takes at most 1,000 UIDs and a list of
{!Imap.Fetch_item.t}. It is one {!Imap_eio.Selected.row} for each UID the
server reported, in request order. A field of a row is [None] when its
item was not requested or the server did not report it.

{[
let archive_old selected =
  let criteria =
    Imap.Search.(And [ Seen; Before { day = 1; month = 1; year = 2025 } ])
  in
  let* uids = Imap_eio.Selected.uid_search selected ~criteria in
  let uids = List.filteri (fun i _ -> i < 1000) uids in
  let* rows =
    Imap_eio.Selected.fetch selected ~uids
      ~items:[ Imap.Fetch_item.Internal_date; Rfc822_size ]
  in
  List.iter
    (fun (row : Imap_eio.Selected.row) ->
      Format.printf "%a %Ld octets@." Imap.Uid.pp row.uid
        (Option.value row.size ~default:0L))
    rows;
  if uids = [] then Ok ()
  else archive selected ~set:(Imap.Uid_set.of_list uids)
]}

{1 Archiving with a fallback}

An operation that exists only because of an extension lives in a
submodule named for it. {!Imap_eio.Selected.Move.require} is a MOVE
witness when the server offers MOVE or IMAP4rev2, and
[Error (Unsupported Move)] otherwise. It sends nothing, so the fallback
is one match arm.

The fallback copies the messages with {!Imap_eio.Selected.uid_copy} and
marks the originals deleted. It checks for CONDSTORE or QRESYNC before
copying, so a server with neither receives no copy.
{!Imap_eio.Selected.Condstore.uid_store_flags} changes only the messages
unchanged since the HIGHESTMODSEQ reported at selection, and [modified]
in its receipt names the UIDs it refused. Expunging the originals is left
to the caller, through {!Imap_eio.Selected.Uidplus.uid_expunge} where the
server offers UIDPLUS.

{[
let ( let* ) = Result.bind

let archive selected ~set =
  let open Imap_eio in
  match Selected.Move.require selected with
  | Ok move ->
      let* _receipt = Selected.Move.uid_move move ~set ~mailbox:"Archive" in
      Ok ()
  | Error (Error.Unsupported _) ->
      let* info = Selected.info selected in
      let* condstore = Selected.Condstore.require selected in
      let* _receipt = Selected.uid_copy selected ~set ~mailbox:"Archive" in
      let* receipt =
        Selected.Condstore.uid_store_flags condstore ~set ~operation:`Add
          ~flags:[ Mail_flag.Imap_flag.system Deleted ]
          ~unchangedsince:(Option.value info.highestmodseq ~default:0L)
      in
      if not (Imap.Uid_set.is_empty receipt.modified) then
        Format.printf "changed since selection: %a@." Imap.Uid_set.pp
          receipt.modified;
      Ok ()
  | Error e -> Error e
]}

{1 Letting Mailbox choose}

{!Imap_eio.Mailbox} makes these choices for a client that is not a
syncer. {!Imap_eio.Mailbox.move} uses MOVE where the server offers it,
else COPY, a STORE adding [\Deleted] and a UIDPLUS UID EXPUNGE of the
same set, else COPY and the STORE alone, which leaves the expunge to the
caller. It returns the strategy with the result. A failure after the
copy is [`Copied] or [`Copied_and_flagged], so the caller knows what to
reconcile. The function below can replace [archive] in [archive_old].

{[
let archive_any selected ~set =
  let open Imap_eio in
  let moved =
    Mailbox.move (Mailbox.of_selected selected) ~set ~mailbox:"Archive"
  in
  let strategy =
    match moved.strategy with
    | `Move -> "MOVE"
    | `Copy_then_expunge -> "COPY, STORE and UID EXPUNGE"
    | `Copy_then_flag -> "COPY and STORE, expunge pending"
    | `Copied _ -> "COPY, then a failed STORE"
    | `Copied_and_flagged _ -> "COPY and STORE, then a failed EXPUNGE"
  in
  Format.printf "archive used %s@." strategy;
  Result.map ignore moved.result
]}

[Error (Uncertain _)] means the server may have applied a command, so
reconcile the mailbox before retrying.
